==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*hek(e)}}; see {{m|la|hic}} for more. Seemingly the more archaic form, retained rarely in Classical Latin as an emphatic variant and reanalysed as {{af|la|hic|-ce}}.

===Adjective===
{{head|la|adjective|feminine|haece|neuter|hoce}}

# {{ngd|Emphatic form of {{m|la|hic}}.}}
#* {{Q|la|Cicero|Pro Lege Manilia|13|18|quote=Itinera quae per '''hosce''' annos in Italia per agros atque oppida civium Romanorum nostri imperatores fecerint, recordamini.|t=Recall the tours our generals have carried out '''these''' years in Italy, through the lands and towns of Roman citizens.}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|la|pronoun|g=m|feminine|haece|neuter|hoce}}

# {{ngd|Emphatic form of {{m|la|hic}}.}}
#* {{Q|la|Accius|Didascalica|1|4|quote=Num ergo aquila ita ut '''hice''' praedicant sciciderat pectus?|t=Surely then an eagle did not tear apart his breast as '''these men''' declare?}}
#* {{Q|la|Gellius|Noctes Atticae|3|16|4|quote=Caecilii versus '''hice''' sunt.|t='''These''' are the lines of Caecilius.}}

